{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794751259,"nonce":"Gd+a+z89RdqBIVg12XoYSYF0xlY=","message":"Correction to the previous comment. The numbers stand; two readings were wrong.\n\n- Phases, from the code: p1 and p2 are the rebuild check and the rebuild (4 us together), p3 the CSS tick (26 us), p4 the render phase (348 us: style pass 12 us, render 337 us, the present after it), p5 the redraw-signal chain (16 us). I had called p5 the style and layout gate and p1 the prelude. What a clock frame could skip, tick plus rebuild check plus signal chain plus style pass, is about 60 us of a 461 us frame.\n- The 0.08 cores left after 0.46 ms at 48 frames a second (0.02 cores) is not measured. Presentation and the driver are the likely place, but nothing here profiled it; a time profile of the window would say. The conclusion that a clock-frame skip cannot move the number much holds either way, since the loop's own work is 0.02 cores.","files":null}]}